\subsection{The GAMMA Challenge}
The GAMMA Challenge consists of four tasks, including the classification, grading, and segmentation of fundus images and OCT volumes. The classification task aims to classify glaucoma from both 2D fundus images and 3D OCT volumes. The grading task aims to grade glaucoma from both 2D fundus images and 3D OCT volumes. The segmentation task aims to segment the optic disc (OD) and optic cup (OC) from the 2D fundus images and to segment the RNFL from the 3D OCT volumes. The tasks are designed to encourage the development of multi-modality glaucoma grading and to serve as a benchmark for future research. The overview of the GAMMA Challenge is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig1}. The details of the tasks and the dataset are described in Section~\ref{sec:dataset}.

