The GAMMA Challenge dataset consists of 2D fundus images and 3D OCT volumes. The 2D fundus images are from the National Eye Institute (NEI) dataset \cite{arxivID-2402.11488-1}, which is a large-scale fundus image dataset with 25,406 images. The 3D OCT volumes are from the Diabetic Retinopathy OCT Dataset (DRIVE) \cite{arxivID-2409.04137-2}, which is a large-scale OCT dataset with 268 volumes. The dataset is annotated by experienced ophthalmologists, and the annotation process is described in Section~\ref{sec:dataset}. The dataset is publicly available on Kaggle\footnote{\href{https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anonymous3345/gamma-challenge}{https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anonymous3345/gamma-challenge}} and GitHub\footnote{\href{https://github.com/Anonymous3345/GAMMA}{https://github.com/Anonymous3345/GAMMA}}.

